FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/property_test.rs:154 — `random_statement` has no arm emitting a bare expression tail, so every generated `Ok` program ends in `set`/`say`/`if`/`repeat` whose value is `nothing` (cf. src/vm.rs:397) — the cross-VM value agreement is vacuous while phases/phase-020/FINDINGS.md §4 records `set t to 5 / say t / t` as `Ok("5")` on one VM and `Ok("nothing")` on the other, and REPORT.md claims 199 `nothing` values are "not a gap" — add a value-bearing tail arm and a corpus family ending in an expression, and assert `tree_walk == bytecode` on it instead of only `tree_walk` vs `.expected` as in tests/differential_test.rs:379.
2. [MAJOR] tests/property_test.rs:117 — `typed_expression` for `Kind::Text` returns `(length(left) + length(left))`, a `Number`, contradicting the `random_statement` contract at tests/property_test.rs:144 that `n`/`t`/`b` keep their types — `set t to <number>` followed by `say length(t)` faults via src/runtime.rs:273, injecting accidental type faults instead of the deliberate `random_fault` mix — return `Text` here (e.g. `("" + ...)` or a text join) so the typed invariant holds.
3. [MINOR] tests/property_test.rs:537 — `candidate.remove(index)` iterates byte indices `0..minimal.len()`, panicking on a non-char-boundary for any multibyte minimal (generator literals include `é`/`🎉` at tests/property_test.rs:138), aborting the test binary instead of failing — iterate `minimal.char_indices().map(|(i,_)| i)` as tests/common/shrink.rs:67 does with `chars`.
4. [MINOR] tests/common/shrink.rs:54 — `candidate.join("\n")` drops a trailing newline (`str::lines` discards it), so every line-based candidate differs from source at EOF and EOF-span cases (`lines+1`, unterminated blocks) shrink against altered input — preserve the terminator (`if source.ends_with('\n') { joined.push('\n') }`).
